  "body": "Currently event handlers are compiled the first time the user agent does 'get the current value of the event handler' (typically when handling the event):\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#getting-the-current-value-of-the-event-handler\r\n\r\nOn the JS side, the created function's ScriptOrModule is set to the result of GetActiveScriptOrModule().  This is used as the context for any dynamic module imports and its URL used to resolve relative module specifiers.\r\n\r\nThe problem is that the active script at this point depends on how the event was triggered.  If it is triggered programmatically by an API then it will be the the calling script, but if it is triggered by a user action there there will be none.\r\n\r\nIt's possible for a handler to be triggered in both ways in a single page (or even from multiple scripts) which could result in it attempting to import from different URLs depending on how it was first triggered.  This seems likely to cause problems.\r\n\r\n/cc @domenic",
